  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A flask contains argon and oxygen in the ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;in mass and the mixture is kept at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The ratio of their average kinetic energy per molecule respectively"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>Ar</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>As argon is monoatomic gas, so it has three degree of freedom <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>f</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and oxygen is a diatomic gas, so its degree of freedom is five.</p><p>We know that average kinetic energy per molecule is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is Boltzmann&#39;s constant and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;is temperature.</p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;is fixed for both gas.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>Ar</mi></msub><msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}